      "status": "posted_exact_readback_verified",
      "authorization": "Daniel explicitly authorized targeted additional outreach in the current conversation on 2026-10-11.",
      "destination": "https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi/issues/799",
      "body": "Hi @zwbx. I'm Daniel, working on deployment debugging in [Nisayon](https://github.com/manfromnowhere143/nisayon). If the WidowX result is still under investigation, I can help check whether the evaluation adapter applies the action conventions used in training.\n\nCould you share the resolved training config and the evaluation adapter at the revisions used for your table? The z-score versus quantile comparison makes the normalization settings particularly useful. If a short saved failing rollout already exists, a few steps containing the input state, policy output and action passed to the environment would help connect the configuration to what actually ran. Existing files or links are fine; a partial record is useful too.\n\nI would start with normalization, action units and ordering, gripper convention, and the number of actions executed per prediction. That inspection could identify a mismatch; whether a correction improves task success would need a subsequent evaluation.\n\nWhich decision is still open for you: change the integration, change the training setup, or something else? The initial check can use existing records without another training run.\n",
      "body_sha256": "b7bca80dbdccf20d6990ac44c6b628d87ec8840b24e1135ede55499ac7878509",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Physical-Intelligence/openpi/issues/799",
