      "status": "posted_exact_readback_verified",
      "authorization": "Daniel explicitly authorized targeted additional outreach in the current conversation on 2026-10-11.",
      "destination": "https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/issues/4633",
      "body": "Hi @NotNANtoN. Do you have the benchmark command and original per-call timing output behind #4634, tied to the tested commit and PyTorch/CUDA versions? The PR and discussion already cover the cache change and the warm-up question. I would like to check what the existing measurements establish for someone deciding whether to enable `compile_denoise`.\n\nI'm Daniel, working on deployment checks in [Nisayon](https://github.com/manfromnowhere143/nisayon). I can review those records and return a short account of the timing boundaries, first-call cost and steady-state distribution, with any missing measurements made explicit. Separating denoising time from complete action prediction would make the comparison easier to use. Existing output is enough to start; this does not require another GPU run.\n\nIs there a current deployment device or decision that such a check would help? I haven't run your benchmark, and a review of the recorded 4090 measurements would leave Jetson performance and task success untested.\n\nI used AI assistance to prepare this request.\n",
      "body_sha256": "e13095994a62167cb91909fac5ae8a9b4fe90c41bd009e7610a182bea3c7cdd2",
